{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/525133-lfg-werewolf-the-forsaken-2ed","id":525133,"title":"[LFG] Werewolf: The Forsaken 2ed","path":["Home","Onyx Path","General","Conventions, Gatherings, and Online Play"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-22T22:19:47-07:00","id":525133,"title":"[LFG] Werewolf: The Forsaken 2ed","content":"I've finally got my paws on the Idigam Chronicles, and now I'm really itching to play a game, especially since I never got to play 1st edition, despite my love for WtF.<br /> <br /> My prefered formata would be PbP, mostly because being European makes playing with US folks (or people from other timezones in general) really hard.<br /> <br /> I'd really love to finally unleash the furry beast I had in mind for a while, but if really no-one wants to ST, I'd be amenable to doing it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/138-bluebiscuit","name":"BlueBiscuit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-22T22:49:26-07:00","id":525167,"title":"","content":"I've been dying to play since the book came out and don't have the time to ST for my usual group right now. But I would love to join a PbP game if there's room for me!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-23T02:13:41-07:00","id":525299,"title":"","content":"I would also be interested in playing. I love the game so much that I literally cannot get enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-23T11:58:10-07:00","id":525761,"title":"","content":"C'mon, no one else? I promise, if by the time we have at least 4 prospective players beside me no steps up to ST the game, I will do it myself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/138-bluebiscuit","name":"BlueBiscuit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-23T12:27:44-07:00","id":525781,"title":"","content":"Two takers in under 24 hours is a good sign, I wouldn't worry too much. This isn't the most highly trafficked subforum, so sometimes it can take a bit. You could try asking in the Forsaken forums if you want to see results faster.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-23T13:55:25-07:00","id":525875,"title":"","content":"Dare I sign up for not one but TWO Werewolf 2e games? Can I handle that much violent furry possibly exploding at any moment? Why I think I can, consider me in if possible. I would prefer not to ST, I'm way too inexperienced at it myself. On the note of getting responses, I'm used to seeing these threads in the PBP forum, which is why I didnt find this one till Charlaquin dropped a post in an old thread of mine. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> As an aside, Blue, wonderful avatar picture. The hype is finally back for his newest addition to the When They Cry Series, heard much on the topic? (If you have no idea what I'm talking about just ignore me. I shall retreat back into my corner of lonliness in regards to Umineko and the When They Cry series...)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1705,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1705-okami","user":"Okami","date":".  Saw Blue Biscuit's avatar picture 05-23-2015, 04:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1705-okami","name":"Okami","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1705_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-23T14:07:39-07:00","id":525904,"title":"","content":"I'm up for this as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-23T14:43:01-07:00","id":525964,"title":"","content":"Well, now I've gotta own up to my words, don't I? <img src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> Still, I'll follow Charlaquins advice and post in the main forums, and see if there are any other applicants, and if anyone else wants to Storytell. As promised though, I'm already thinking about what sort of game I want to pitch to you. I'm open to advice from more experienced WtF STs.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Okami</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/525133-lfg-werewolf-the-forsaken-2ed?p=525875#post525875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As an aside, Blue, wonderful avatar picture. The hype is finally back for his newest addition to the When They Cry Series, heard much on the topic? (If you have no idea what I'm talking about just ignore me. I shall retreat back into my corner of lonliness in regards to Umineko and the When They Cry series...)</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, I'm curious though, what kind of news? PM me, maybe?<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/138-bluebiscuit","name":"BlueBiscuit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-23T20:17:33-07:00","id":526268,"title":"","content":"I'm game. I'll probably be the Sandman.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-23T20:57:52-07:00","id":526331,"title":"","content":"I'd like to do a play-by-post. I'm in a secluded part of the country for the next few months so my opportunities for RPGs are limited.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/233-daydreamer","name":"Daydreamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"193"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-23T21:07:22-07:00","id":526334,"title":"","content":"That makes six of us, not counting Blue Biscut, which was his preferred cap. Unless someone else offers to ST and is cool with more players.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-23T21:12:24-07:00","id":526340,"title":"","content":"Indeed, I was just about to say, unless anyone else steps forth, this is it for player spots, and once I manage to catch some zzzs, I guess we can start pitching Chronicle ideas from my side and character concepts from yours, if everyone is fine with that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/138-bluebiscuit","name":"BlueBiscuit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-23T21:38:54-07:00","id":526363,"title":"","content":"Never done pbp, but I'm interested, if there is still room.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1840-akashicmonk","name":"akashicmonk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1840_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-23T21:46:55-07:00","id":526367,"title":"","content":"Unless you're offering to Storytell, we already have all 6 slots spoken for, sorry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/138-bluebiscuit","name":"BlueBiscuit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-23T21:50:39-07:00","id":526369,"title":"","content":"No worries.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1840-akashicmonk","name":"akashicmonk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1840_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-24T07:23:33-07:00","id":526631,"title":"","content":"I think I'd like to hear about the chronicle's general idea and setting before I come up with a character. I don't want to dream up someone I really want to play and then find out they're not a good match for the chronicle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/233-daydreamer","name":"Daydreamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"193"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-24T07:58:00-07:00","id":526646,"title":"","content":"Agreed, though I'd be lying if I said I didnt have someone in mind already and the character is still in its flexible stages, so I have my hopes somewhat up. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1705-okami","name":"Okami","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1705_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-24T08:02:58-07:00","id":526665,"title":"","content":"I've gotten down on paper the crunchy parts of the character I want to run, but I'm still working on personality and backstory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-24T09:01:22-07:00","id":526728,"title":"","content":"I've got a good start on an Irraka Hunter in Darkness, though I'm waiting to finalize details until I've seen if he'll be a good fit for the group and the chronicle. Currently I'm thinking of playing a character who was homeless prior to his First Change, and took it as kind of a blessing when he became a werewolf. He could make his territory his home, and hunt when ever he needed food. The Hunters in Darkness were a natural fit for him, with their emphasis on protecting one's territory.<br /> <br /> I also don't want to settle on Merits before discussing any shared Merits we might want (Safe Place, Dedicated Locus, Residential Area, Totem, etc.) and who's investing what into them. Though I know I want at least a few dots of Anonymity if I go with this character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-24T09:22:18-07:00","id":526760,"title":"","content":"Fair, I'm curious to see how shared merits works out too, I know in the game I'm currently in we're going to hunt our totem, so we couldnt invest in the merit at all. It's odd, the character I'm working on his linked to the one I'm currently using (working on him made me interested in this one). She's also a Bone Shadow, but I want to avoid going Ithaeur again if I can, gonna re-read and see if any Auspice fits her better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1705-okami","name":"Okami","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1705_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-24T10:00:47-07:00","id":526804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Okami</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/525133-lfg-werewolf-the-forsaken-2ed?p=526760#post526760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fair, I'm curious to see how shared merits works out too, I know in the game I'm currently in we're going to hunt our totem, so we couldnt invest in the merit at all. It's odd, the character I'm working on his linked to the one I'm currently using (working on him made me interested in this one). She's also a Bone Shadow, but I want to avoid going Ithaeur again if I can, gonna re-read and see if any Auspice fits her better.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting. Did you all just get your free Totem dot after catching it? I wouldn't mind playing out acquiring the totem in-game, but I wouldn't want to lose the free dot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-24T10:52:42-07:00","id":526833,"title":"","content":"Ok then, got a few hours of sleep, can think clearly now. This is all really early thoughts, and as I've said, I'm open to suggestions<br /> <br /> What I've got so far in terms of ideas:<br /> Set in a yet to be named fictional city, the theme of this Chronicle would be &quot;A Forsaken Life&quot;, with the pack having to deal with and Hunte humans, Spirits, Claimed, Hosts and other Uratha, both Pure and Forsaken, and the relationships that they form with them, the whole gamut that a Forsaken pack could have to deal with. Mood would be &quot;Something big is going on&quot;, an undercurrent of something greater going on behind the scenes, right from the start, slowing unfolding into a clearer picture in front of the pack.<br /> <br /> I could see this chronicle starting with either the pack already formed and bound through a Totem, or with your characters meeting each other for the first time and going on their first Hunt togheter as a pack, perhaps with some elder or experienced pack &quot;sponsoring&quot; you for a certain territory, a la Max Roman in Denver.<br /> <br /> For the Setting, as I've been running M&amp;M for my RL group recently, I've got their city book &quot;Emerald City&quot; on my mind lately, so I'm thinking about the coast of the Pacific Northwest, with the environment being a mix between deeply urbanised in the city proper and wilderness, with forests and mountains, perhaps a National Park. There are some things I'd also like in the Hunting Grounds of the corebook that I'd like to incorporate, on some level. Will expand on this later, if we end up playing this chronicle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":138,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/138-bluebiscuit","user":"BlueBiscuit","date":". 05-24-2015, 01:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/138-bluebiscuit","name":"BlueBiscuit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-24T11:12:57-07:00","id":526846,"title":"","content":"I'm cool with playing an already established pack or meeting and forming a pack in-game, though I think the latter seems like it fits the &quot;Forsaken Life&quot; theme a bit better in my opinion. If we did it that way though, I might like to make a character fresh off her First Change, still struggling to come to terms with being a werewolf and to find her place in Uratha culture. But that's a concept that could potentially cause a lot of friction with the rest of the pack, so I'd only do that if everyone else is cool with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-24T14:00:50-07:00","id":527009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/525133-lfg-werewolf-the-forsaken-2ed?p=526804#post526804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting. Did you all just get your free Totem dot after catching it? I wouldn't mind playing out acquiring the totem in-game, but I wouldn't want to lose the free dot.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm assuming we will, havent got that far actually.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BlueBiscuit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/525133-lfg-werewolf-the-forsaken-2ed?p=526833#post526833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok then, got a few hours of sleep, can think clearly now. This is all really early thoughts, and as I've said, I'm open to suggestions<br /> <br /> What I've got so far in terms of ideas:<br /> Set in a yet to be named fictional city, the theme of this Chronicle would be &quot;A Forsaken Life&quot;, with the pack having to deal with and Hunte humans, Spirits, Claimed, Hosts and other Uratha, both Pure and Forsaken, and the relationships that they form with them, the whole gamut that a Forsaken pack could have to deal with. Mood would be &quot;Something big is going on&quot;, an undercurrent of something greater going on behind the scenes, right from the start, slowing unfolding into a clearer picture in front of the pack.<br /> <br /> I could see this chronicle starting with either the pack already formed and bound through a Totem, or with your characters meeting each other for the first time and going on their first Hunt togheter as a pack, perhaps with some elder or experienced pack &quot;sponsoring&quot; you for a certain territory, a la Max Roman in Denver.<br /> <br /> For the Setting, as I've been running M&amp;M for my RL group recently, I've got their city book &quot;Emerald City&quot; on my mind lately, so I'm thinking about the coast of the Pacific Northwest, with the environment being a mix between deeply urbanised in the city proper and wilderness, with forests and mountains, perhaps a National Park. There are some things I'd also like in the Hunting Grounds of the corebook that I'd like to incorporate, on some level. Will expand on this later, if we end up playing this chronicle.</div> </div> </div> </div>This setting sounds great, like Char I'm cool with either and agree that the latter would fit the theme better. I see my character as someone whose been Uratha for a while, enough to have shown a younger Bone Shadow the ropes, but has yet to settle with a pack until now. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1705-okami","name":"Okami","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1705_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-24T14:10:18-07:00","id":527043,"title":"","content":"I am thinking of playing a Storm Lord Elodoth or Cahalith. Trying to stay away from my usual Irraka default. I'm down to play either an established pack or a bunch of newbies. I'm also cool with fresh off the boat Uratha. Was thinking of maybe making one myself, depending on whether we go with established or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-24T14:22:55-07:00","id":527051,"title":"","content":"Another rough idea for a chronicle I've got is one more along the lines of the Colorado Springs demo.<br /> <br /> Basically, until recently, the city was primarily Forsaken territory, with several packs making alliances, feuding and competing with each other. Nothing peacful, for peace is almost unknown to the children of Mother Wolf, but, in some way, harmonious. Until <i>something </i>happened, and Uratha started being killed. Blame for the killings began being tossed around the Uratha community, and in short time there was a re-enactment of the brethren war, leaving most Forsaken vulnerable to their enemies; soon, the city was mostly devoid Uratha of the Moon Tribes.<br /> <br /> Here is where you come in; some of you could be survivors of the massacre, having being saved by your older packmates when you where just a freshly changed pup and sent away from the city; maybe you were a Ghost Wolf at the time, and had the good sense of getting out of dodge before the going got too brutal; maybe you have never even been there before, but the story of the events has moved you, perhaps out of desire to redeem the failures of the fallen, or to anger at their death at the hands of traitorous spirits or the claws of the Anshega.<br /> Whatever your reason, you have joined togheter as a pack, under the auspices of the elders of your packs and tribes, with the intention of carving your own path in a dangerous land.<br /> <br /> This chronicle is still pretty vague in my head beyond the starting point, but perhaps it doesn't have to be too neat. It would be a Saints Row/The Shield/Daredevil kind of chronicle, with sort of a gang warfare feel to it, as the characters pack conquers territory, makes connections and defend what they have obtained.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":138,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/138-bluebiscuit","user":"BlueBiscuit","date":". 05-24-2015, 05:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/138-bluebiscuit","name":"BlueBiscuit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-24T14:41:05-07:00","id":527056,"title":"","content":"Is that more specifics on the earlier idea you proposed, or a separate pitch?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-24T14:43:00-07:00","id":527058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/525133-lfg-werewolf-the-forsaken-2ed?p=527056#post527056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is that more specifics on the earlier idea you proposed, or a separate pitch?</div> </div> </div> </div>A different idea that came to me while eating dinner. Just wanted to put it down before it got away from me, but it could easily be rolled over and united with the previous pitch, which I see has been liked so far.<br /> <br /> Edit: It also seems that at least two of you are interested in playing relatively new Uratha, so I guess that whatever chronicle pitch gets picked, it's going to being with the meeting of the character and creation of the pack.<br /> As for the Totem and the merit poins that you will eventually assing to it, I'm of the opinion that at chargen you can &quot;bank&quot; the amount of points that you wish to dedicate to your Totem, but even if you choose to not do so, you will still get the free point and the pack benefit, if that makes sense?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":138,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/138-bluebiscuit","user":"BlueBiscuit","date":". 05-24-2015, 06:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/138-bluebiscuit","name":"BlueBiscuit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-24T15:22:02-07:00","id":527084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BlueBiscuit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/525133-lfg-werewolf-the-forsaken-2ed?p=527058#post527058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A different idea that came to me while eating dinner. Just wanted to put it down before it got away from me, but it could easily be rolled over and united with the previous pitch, which I see has been liked so far.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cool, just making sure. I definitely like the first idea a lot, and I could see the second being rolled into it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BlueBiscuit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/525133-lfg-werewolf-the-forsaken-2ed?p=527058#post527058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edit: It also seems that at least two of you are interested in playing relatively new Uratha, so I guess that whatever chronicle pitch gets picked, it's going to being with the meeting of the character and creation of the pack.<br /> As for the Totem and the merit poins that you will eventually assing to it, I'm of the opinion that at chargen you can &quot;bank&quot; the amount of points that you wish to dedicate to your Totem, but even if you choose to not do so, you will still get the free point and the pack benefit, if that makes sense?</div> </div> </div> </div>Cool beans. That makes sense to me and seems like a good way to run it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 05-24-2015, 06:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-24T15:30:41-07:00","id":527090,"title":"","content":"I've settled on a Bone Shadow Elodoth, who started out as a two-bit, Phonebook Psychic until his First Change. I've kind of built him as a Social/Gather Info specialist. I've already set aside some Merit dots for Totem, but if we're going to go through the process IC, I might switch for Hobbyist Clique and/or Esoteric Armory, if allowed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-24T15:49:24-07:00","id":527115,"title":"","content":"The search and hunt for the Totem is something that I'd like to see done IC, but the mechanical aspects are best handled previously OOC. As I've said, even if you elect to not reserve any point to the Totem, you will still get the free 1 dot, which in this case would represent the fact that you have partecipated and contributed in the hunting and binding of the spirit.<br /> <br /> Anyway, as soon as I can I will post a short writeup of the setting. I'll try to follow the format of the Hunting Grounds of the core, with things like Packs, Prey and Locations in it. Hopefully, it should help with backstory hooks and ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/138-bluebiscuit","name":"BlueBiscuit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-24T15:53:21-07:00","id":527118,"title":"","content":"Hmm, the more I mull this character around the more she's so difficult. She knows spirits, but she's more a, well, scientist than a shaman. In the hunt she uses knowledge, rites, and bullets. is she an Ithaeur or a Bone Shadow? I'd prefer she not be both, but she might be.<br /> <br /> Edit; What if she's neither? Just someone who made it her business to know spirits cold. As an Uratha that's only the smart thing to do, and she has a habit of separating people into those who are 'fools' and those who aren't.<br /> <br /> Also, ignore me, I'm just sounding out my own ideas <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1705,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1705-okami","user":"Okami","date":". 05-24-2015, 07:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1705-okami","name":"Okami","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1705_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-24T15:57:03-07:00","id":527119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Okami</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/525133-lfg-werewolf-the-forsaken-2ed?p=527118#post527118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, the more I mull this character around the more she's so difficult. She knows spirits, but she's more a, well, scientist than a shaman. In the hunt she uses knowledge, rites, and bullets. is she an Ithaeur or a Bone Shadow? I'd prefer she not be both, but she might be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yay, a colleague.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-24T16:00:14-07:00","id":527121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/525133-lfg-werewolf-the-forsaken-2ed?p=527090#post527090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've settled on a Bone Shadow Elodoth, who started out as a two-bit, Phonebook Psychic until his First Change. I've kind of built him as a Social/Gather Info specialist. I've already set aside some Merit dots for Totem, but if we're going to go through the process IC, I might switch for Hobbyist Clique and/or Esoteric Armory, if allowed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Definitely Esoteric Armory 2. I like being prepared.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-24T16:02:14-07:00","id":527124,"title":"","content":"Personally, I like the second pitch because it seems more focused. We have a clear goal to achieve, a mystery to solve that takes center stage.<br /> <br /> I think I'd like to roll a Rahu character. I was thinking of a wanderer who's tired of being a rootless Ghost Wolf and wants to find a pack and a permanent home. He doesn't talk at all about his life before he became a drifter, and he seems to know an awful lot about how the Pure operate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/233-daydreamer","name":"Daydreamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"193"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-24T16:06:42-07:00","id":527126,"title":"","content":"Esoteric Armory seems to me be something like any Uratha that likes do be rough with spirits, or is just paranoid about them, would either have or accumulate with time, so I don't see reason to disallow it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/138-bluebiscuit","name":"BlueBiscuit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-24T16:12:29-07:00","id":527134,"title":"","content":"Thinking on it, would anyone object to my character starting off as a Wolf-Blooded and First Changing in-game? Maybe using the Tension Pool rules to help facilitate that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-24T16:20:31-07:00","id":527141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daydreamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/525133-lfg-werewolf-the-forsaken-2ed?p=527124#post527124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I like the second pitch because it seems more focused. We have a clear goal to achieve, a mystery to solve that takes center stage.<br /> <br /> I think I'd like to roll a Rahu character. I was thinking of a wanderer who's tired of being a rootless Ghost Wolf and wants to find a pack and a permanent home. He doesn't talk at all about his life before he became a drifter, and he seems to know an awful lot about how the Pure operate.</div> </div> </div> </div>As Charlaquin pointed out, it should be fairly easy to roll up those two togheter, especially as the first is built to be more of a Sandbox, which doesn't preclude at all the more focused narrative of the second chronicle idea, which is what you like.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/525133-lfg-werewolf-the-forsaken-2ed?p=527134#post527134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thinking on it, would anyone object to my character starting off as a Wolf-Blooded and First Changing in-game? Maybe using the Tension Pool rules to help facilitate that?</div> </div> </div> </div>If everyone is fine with it, I've got no objection. It would actually fit pretty well with what I have in mind for the kickstart of the chronicle, and truth to be told I've always wanted to play/run a Tribal Initiation, when and if you get that far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/138-bluebiscuit","name":"BlueBiscuit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-24T16:27:27-07:00","id":527145,"title":"","content":"That would be awesome! I'll start work on the character assuming that'll be her arc, and if anyone would rather not deal with the complications such a character might cause, I totally understand. Just say the word and I'll use my Hunter in Darkness character instead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-24T16:43:42-07:00","id":527156,"title":"","content":"Cool. I'm almost ready to go.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-24T16:56:01-07:00","id":527162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/525133-lfg-werewolf-the-forsaken-2ed?p=527145#post527145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That would be awesome! I'll start work on the character assuming that'll be her arc, and if anyone would rather not deal with the complications such a character might cause, I totally understand. Just say the word and I'll use my Hunter in Darkness character instead.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Go for it, my character would likely try and pull being an odd sort of mentor, depending on whether she takes an interest in your character or not, and provided thats ok with you of course.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/525133-lfg-werewolf-the-forsaken-2ed?p=527121#post527121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Definitely Esoteric Armory 2. I like being prepared.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didnt even know this was a merit. Where did you find this? I'd have my character go for it but moving a lot means little baggae, thniking she knows more of how to craft this kind of stuff than has it on hand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1705,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1705-okami","user":"Okami","date":". 05-24-2015, 07:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1705-okami","name":"Okami","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1705_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-24T17:05:04-07:00","id":527165,"title":"","content":"You can find Esoteric Armory in the GMC rules update, page 231.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/138-bluebiscuit","name":"BlueBiscuit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-24T17:08:34-07:00","id":527168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Okami</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/525133-lfg-werewolf-the-forsaken-2ed?p=527162#post527162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didnt even know this was a merit. Where did you find this? I'd have my character go for it but moving a lot means little baggae, thniking she knows more of how to craft this kind of stuff than has it on hand.</div> </div> </div> </div>God Machine Chronicle, in the Appendix, in the Ephemeral Beings section, in a sidebar after the section on Interaction with Mortals, pg. 231.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-24T18:19:16-07:00","id":527221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Okami</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/525133-lfg-werewolf-the-forsaken-2ed?p=527162#post527162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Go for it, my character would likely try and pull being an odd sort of mentor, depending on whether she takes an interest in your character or not, and provided thats ok with you of course.</div> </div> </div> </div>Definitely! She'll probably need someone to help steer her towards balancing her Harmony, so that would probably work well.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Okami</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/525133-lfg-werewolf-the-forsaken-2ed?p=527162#post527162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didnt even know this was a merit. Where did you find this? I'd have my character go for it but moving a lot means little baggae, thniking she knows more of how to craft this kind of stuff than has it on hand.</div> </div> </div> </div>For some reason GMC had like three Merits that weren't in the actual Merit section. This, Virtuous, and Vice-Ridden.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-24T18:24:58-07:00","id":527222,"title":"","content":"Before I roll this Rahu up, I'd just like to make sure that no one has a problem with these traits: 1. Starting out as a Ghost Wolf. 2. Having his backstory being a secret known only to myself and BlueBiscuit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/233-daydreamer","name":"Daydreamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"193"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-24T18:36:33-07:00","id":527225,"title":"","content":"Being a Ghost Wolf is absolutely no problem, we already have Wolf-Blooded that will Change in play, after all. As for the backstory, you're all free to keep elements of your character's history from each other to any extent you wish, though I will still need to know and approve it of course.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/138-bluebiscuit","name":"BlueBiscuit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-24T19:35:32-07:00","id":527251,"title":"","content":"I sent you a PM with the gist of it. If it sounds good, I can give you a more detailed version.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/233-daydreamer","name":"Daydreamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"193"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T09:46:32-07:00","id":527792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Okami</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/525133-lfg-werewolf-the-forsaken-2ed?p=527118#post527118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, the more I mull this character around the more she's so difficult. She knows spirits, but she's more a, well, scientist than a shaman. In the hunt she uses knowledge, rites, and bullets. is she an Ithaeur or a Bone Shadow? I'd prefer she not be both, but she might be.<br /> <br /> Edit; What if she's neither? Just someone who made it her business to know spirits cold. As an Uratha that's only the smart thing to do, and she has a habit of separating people into those who are 'fools' and those who aren't.<br /> <br /> Also, ignore me, I'm just sounding out my own ideas <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This sounds more like a Ithaeur Iron Master.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T09:47:41-07:00","id":527793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daydreamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/525133-lfg-werewolf-the-forsaken-2ed?p=527124#post527124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I like the second pitch because it seems more focused. We have a clear goal to achieve, a mystery to solve that takes center stage.<br /> <br /> I think I'd like to roll a Rahu character. I was thinking of a wanderer who's tired of being a rootless Ghost Wolf and wants to find a pack and a permanent home. He doesn't talk at all about his life before he became a drifter, and he seems to know an awful lot about how the Pure operate.</div> </div> </div> </div>The second pitch seems more like something to look at IC, a plot Hook, IMO. Something that the characters might be able to prevent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T09:49:20-07:00","id":527794,"title":"","content":"I think I'll go Blood Talon Rahu gang-banger.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T10:05:49-07:00","id":527809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/525133-lfg-werewolf-the-forsaken-2ed?p=527792#post527792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> This sounds more like a Ithaeur Iron Master.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You may or may not have read my mind, as I've been working on her sheet I've noticed she fights like an Irraka (in the sense that she prefers quick kills from stealth and preferably ranged using bullets) except she actually pays attention to the spirit world, and the iron master oath resonates more with her than the Hunters In Darkness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1705-okami","name":"Okami","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1705_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T11:37:38-07:00","id":527912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/525133-lfg-werewolf-the-forsaken-2ed?p=527794#post527794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I'll go Blood Talon Rahu gang-banger.</div> </div> </div> </div>Scratch this. What do we have so far? Elodoth, Irraka, Ithaeur, Rahu? Missing Cahalith?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T12:00:39-07:00","id":527939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/525133-lfg-werewolf-the-forsaken-2ed?p=527912#post527912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Scratch this. What do we have so far? Elodoth, Irraka, Ithaeur, Rahu? Missing Cahalith?</div> </div> </div> </div>We've got Elodoth, Rahu, Ithaeur, and undecided Elodoth or Cahalith. My character's Auspice will be determined by the moon phase when she First Changes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T12:05:59-07:00","id":527946,"title":"","content":"I was working on an Elodoth/Cahalith Storm Lord. I think I'm leaning a bit more towards Cahalith just for the purposes of role diversity (since my character is sounding a lot like Hexmeister Vic's). But if you're going with a Cahalith maybe it'll tip the scales back. Keep in mind, with six of us we are going to end up with overlap no matter what we do, so that's fine too.<br /> <br /> My character is either:<br /> <br /> A social manipulator type who uses information to get whatever she wants, sort of an information dealer who knows anybody and everybody. (Various street level Contacts, Fast Talking merit, Fixer merit, Prey on Weakness, Primal Allure, Strings of the Heart merit, etc.) - Elodoth<br /> <br /> Or a gregarious street/underground fighter who is a bit famous in certain circles, and enjoys all the benefits of his minor celebrity. (1-2 dots in fame, Barfly merit, War Howl, Song in Your Heart merit, etc.) - Cahalith<br /> <br /> Also in the end I may just scrap all that for an Irraka because I love Irraka.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T12:29:07-07:00","id":527997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/525133-lfg-werewolf-the-forsaken-2ed?p=527946#post527946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was working on an Elodoth/Cahalith Storm Lord. I think I'm leaning a bit more towards Cahalith just for the purposes of role diversity (since my character is sounding a lot like Hexmeister Vic's). But if you're going with a Cahalith maybe it'll tip the scales back. Keep in mind, with six of us we are going to end up with overlap no matter what we do, so that's fine too.<br /> <br /> My character is either:<br /> <br /> A social manipulator type who uses information to get whatever she wants, sort of an information dealer who knows anybody and everybody. (Various street level Contacts, Fast Talking merit, Fixer merit, Prey on Weakness, Primal Allure, Strings of the Heart merit, etc.) - Elodoth<br /> <br /> Or a gregarious street/underground fighter who is a bit famous in certain circles, and enjoys all the benefits of his minor celebrity. (1-2 dots in fame, Barfly merit, War Howl, Song in Your Heart merit, etc.) - Cahalith<br /> <br /> Also in the end I may just scrap all that for an Irraka because I love Irraka.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like all of these character concepts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T12:52:37-07:00","id":528018,"title":"","content":"So far as rites go, where's everyone sitting? I'm thinking of picking up messenger and chain rage","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1705-okami","name":"Okami","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1705_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T13:11:44-07:00","id":528034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/525133-lfg-werewolf-the-forsaken-2ed?p=527912#post527912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Scratch this. What do we have so far? Elodoth, Irraka, Ithaeur, Rahu? Missing Cahalith?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm rolling Rahu, but the concept I have in mind is a bit more defensive than the usual combat-monkey. He likes to pick his battles and prefers a rope-a-dope strategy when he can make it work, letting his enemies wear themselves out until they present him with an opening. If you want to roll up a berserker Rahu whose best defense is a good offense, that would minimize the overlap between us.<br /> <br /> By the way, Blue, if you haven't thought of a name for this city already, I think &quot;<a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Willapa_people\" target=\"_blank\">Willapa</a>&quot; could work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":233,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/233-daydreamer","user":"Daydreamer","date":". 05-25-2015, 04:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/233-daydreamer","name":"Daydreamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"193"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T13:28:01-07:00","id":528045,"title":"","content":"So, this Wolf-blooded character is not cooperating with me. She needs more time to cook, so I'll just roll my Irraka Hunter for this game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T15:58:44-07:00","id":528160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/525133-lfg-werewolf-the-forsaken-2ed?p=528045#post528045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, this Wolf-blooded character is not cooperating with me. She needs more time to cook, so I'll just roll my Irraka Hunter for this game.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sadface, would have been an interesting character to play with, never worked with a wolf blooded before. Sure you dont want to just sleep on it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1705-okami","name":"Okami","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1705_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T16:05:52-07:00","id":528178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Okami</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/525133-lfg-werewolf-the-forsaken-2ed?p=528160#post528160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sadface, would have been an interesting character to play with, never worked with a wolf blooded before. Sure you dont want to just sleep on it?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll give her some more thought, for sure. I've got the other guy finished (pending ST approval, of course) and ready as a backup, so I guess I've got some time to keep fiddling with her.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T17:59:53-07:00","id":528306,"title":"","content":"Sorry if it seems like I'm stalling. I just keep going over changing stuff, but in my head and in parts already written down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/138-bluebiscuit","name":"BlueBiscuit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T18:27:11-07:00","id":528335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Okami</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/525133-lfg-werewolf-the-forsaken-2ed?p=528018#post528018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So far as rites go, where's everyone sitting? I'm thinking of picking up messenger and chain rage</div> </div> </div> </div>Totemic Empowerment, Banish, and Bottle Spirit. Got a lot of <i>Geasa </i>under the hood as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":1959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","user":"Hexmeister Vic","date":". 05-26-2015, 04:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T19:07:06-07:00","id":528376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/525133-lfg-werewolf-the-forsaken-2ed?p=527997#post527997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I like all of these character concepts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks. I still am no closer to making a decision, though. Sort of waiting to see everyone else's I guess, and what fits best.<br /> <br /> As far as rites, I'm thinking of getting Hunting Grounds or Moon's Mad Love (again depending on the character). Are you allowed to start with fetishes in 2e or no? I can't find anything that says you can, but if anyone knows better I'd love to know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T19:12:53-07:00","id":528378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/525133-lfg-werewolf-the-forsaken-2ed?p=528376#post528376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanks. I still am no closer to making a decision, though. Sort of waiting to see everyone else's I guess, and what fits best.<br /> <br /> As far as rites, I'm thinking of getting Hunting Grounds or Moon's Mad Love (again depending on the character). Are you allowed to start with fetishes in 2e or no? I can't find anything that says you can, but if anyone knows better I'd love to know.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's no rule for starting with Fetishes. They have to be made with the Rite or acquired in-game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T19:28:19-07:00","id":528385,"title":"","content":"If anyone's running into a block with Blood and Bone archetypes, I think <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/432182-new-blood-and-bone-archetypes\">this old thread</a> will be useful. It's sure helping me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/233-daydreamer","name":"Daydreamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"193"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T19:38:26-07:00","id":528412,"title":"","content":"That's what I figured. Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T09:36:44-07:00","id":528840,"title":"","content":"So how are we handling gear and whatnot? Do we enter with anything, procure everything in character...?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1705-okami","name":"Okami","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1705_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T10:21:53-07:00","id":528918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Okami</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/525133-lfg-werewolf-the-forsaken-2ed?p=528840#post528840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So how are we handling gear and whatnot? Do we enter with anything, procure everything in character...?</div> </div> </div> </div>I've always based what I'd have on my Resources, if it was important to my character build, but since I'm not playing a dedicated combat character this time around, I didn't take any. So I'm curious, are we allowed to use mechanically inconsequential equipment for stuff that has little to no bearing on our character's functionality, or do we need to have Resources or other Merits to justify having equipment?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T10:46:31-07:00","id":528954,"title":"","content":"As unhelpful as it may sounds, the way I run it is &quot;anything goes, as long as it makes sense&quot;. Resources is a good guideline, since it's meant to represent a steady source of income, as are the appropriate social Merits, but it's not a hard rule. Let's just say that if you can find it commonly avaible and it's under 60 bucks, you can have it.<br /> Besides that, I'll make other calls based on the particulars of the character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/138-bluebiscuit","name":"BlueBiscuit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T11:23:07-07:00","id":529041,"title":"","content":"I need nothing, save maybe a set of Throwing Knives.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T11:50:29-07:00","id":529076,"title":"","content":"Here is a copy of my character sheet. I haven't written a detailed backstory yet, but I'm working on it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0BwaVV2Oc5KiIeDZoRDNTbnVyT00/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0BwaVV2Oc5KiIeDZoRDNTbnVyT00/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0BwaVV2Oc5KiIeDZoRDNTbnVyT00/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> https://drive.google.com/file/d/0BwaVV2Oc5KiIeDZoRDNTbnVyT00/view?usp=sharing </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T13:31:25-07:00","id":529197,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0BxK0La5plUm8QmJ2NzFFTUowVkU/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Here is the sheet for my character</a>. Tentative.<br /> <br /> Might change gift/facet from Primal Allure to Deny Everything. Might drop Striking Looks for another dot in Contacts. Willing to drop a dot or two for Totem, depending on how we are handling this. And still trying to figure out the right balance in the social skills section. Also thinking of adding Alternate Identity to the list of merits somehow, haha. I'm starved for merits dots/experience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","user":"Amravanti","date":". 05-26-2015, 04:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T08:58:26-07:00","id":530009,"title":"","content":"I would like to join, but at the moment, I don't know anything about the 2nd edition. Anyway I'm familiar with the first one if it can help...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T09:19:59-07:00","id":530041,"title":"","content":"We've filled up on spots unfortunately Impergi, Amravanti I'm hitting the same wall in terms of merit fiddling, should have a tentative sheet up by today.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1705-okami","name":"Okami","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1705_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T09:20:43-07:00","id":530042,"title":"","content":"We should have that pack building session, if characters are more or less fleshed out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T09:27:24-07:00","id":530047,"title":"","content":"I've got my stats all figured out for the Wolf-Blooded, still working on background. I'll post a character sheet soon, I convinced Mr. Gone to make an unofficial character sheet for Wolf-Blooded PCs, so I'm planning to use that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/525133-lfg-werewolf-the-forsaken-2ed?p=530042#post530042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We should have that pack building session, if characters are more or less fleshed out.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, but we should also keep in mind we're planning to actually form the pack in-game. Some of our characters have probably never met, and we don't have a Totem yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T09:30:03-07:00","id":530052,"title":"","content":"Ok... Count me out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T09:36:42-07:00","id":530059,"title":"","content":"I mean, if that's a deal breaker for you, we can discuss the option of being an already-formed pack. I just assumed since no one objected when we were discussing the idea a few pages back that everyone was cool with it. I've got no problem with playing a pre-existing pack, although in that case I'd prefer to play a werewolf rather than a Wolf-Blooded.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T09:55:08-07:00","id":530076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/525133-lfg-werewolf-the-forsaken-2ed?p=530059#post530059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, if that's a deal breaker for you, we can discuss the option of being an already-formed pack. I just assumed since no one objected when we were discussing the idea a few pages back that everyone was cool with it. I've got no problem with playing a pre-existing pack, although in that case I'd prefer to play a werewolf rather than a Wolf-Blooded.</div> </div> </div> </div>Either way is good with me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T10:01:04-07:00","id":530081,"title":"","content":"Blue, would you want us to sketch up some Wolf-blooded, mundane human, and/or supernatural (spirits, wolves, that guy that just won't die or contract Lunacy) NPC packmates?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T10:03:14-07:00","id":530086,"title":"","content":"So the party is full...? I'm a little sad but it cannot be helped... anyway let me know if things change...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T10:23:33-07:00","id":530102,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I don't know that any of us were dead set on that (correct me if I'm wrong), I think it was a suggestion that no one appeared to object to. So like Charlaquin said, if that's a deal breaker for you I have literally zero problem playing a more established pack.<br /> <br /> As far as periphery pack characters, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0BxK0La5plUm8aVRCWlZKTTJvZlU/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">here is my current idea for one</a>, though anything that comes up through brain storming our pack creation process might change that. Which is actually my favourite part of 2e so I'm ready to get that going.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I am imagining him as her brother, sort of a huge, intimidating guy. Mostly because my character being as frail as she is, she'd have to have had some muscle help to keep safe with all the secrets she has/blackmailing she has going on. She's bound to have gotten herself in trouble from time to time. And I just like the contrast. Alternatively she could have had a partner in crime within the pack, but no one sounds like they are the kind of guy that would partner with her yet, so I'm thinking this was who she was before the first change and her brother has always been the other half to the coin.<br /> <br /> I'm imagining that they come from a family of criminals. Either from a prominent crime (organized) family that self destructed due to infighting, or just a family of career criminals. They themselves aren't strictly criminals (not in the traditional sense), but they skirt the line very closely. Current ideas I have are that they have a grudge with the mayor for some reason and are working to take him down, and their father was claimed at some point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T10:30:41-07:00","id":530111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/525133-lfg-werewolf-the-forsaken-2ed?p=530081#post530081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Blue, would you want us to sketch up some Wolf-blooded, mundane human, and/or supernatural (spirits, wolves, that guy that just won't die or contract Lunacy) NPC packmates?</div> </div> </div> </div>It depends. If we end up with starting as an already formed pack then sure, just follow the pack creation guidelines. If we end up instead with the previous proposal of beginning with all of your characters starting separately and then forming the pack, I guess it could still work? They would be &quot;Pack candidates&quot; NPCs rather and true packmates, as of course the entire pack should agree IC as to who allow to join their pack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/138-bluebiscuit","name":"BlueBiscuit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T12:01:45-07:00","id":530179,"title":"","content":"Oh, wow, I assumed the majority of the pack had been formed for a bit and we had just accepted Charlaquin's recently changed character, so apparently we're all over the board here. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I'm ok with doing it however is best for everyone, so lets see what options have been put on the table;<br /> <br /> 1) None or perhaps a couple members of the pack know each each other, we have no totem, we form the pack in game and hunt it.<br /> <br /> 2) The pack is already established and we have no Totem, play starts with us hunting one.<br /> <br /> 3) Both the Pack and the Totem are established<br /> <br /> 4) As 2, except we have been watching a wolf-blooded (only if Charlaquin likes the idea and wish's to use their wolf-blooded character) for some time and their change has finally happened. We start tracking down the new Uratha and induct them into the pack. (possible competition with Pure here?)<br /> <br /> 5) As 3, with 4 thrown in, again only provided all players are on-board with the notion.<br /> <br /> 6) As 1, including 4 but strike the &quot;as 2&quot; claus)<br /> <br /> I'm not saying these are the only options we have to choose from, but what's possible based on what I've seen discussed here. First, lets rule out any options that are enough to make a player quit the campaign entirely. So far Ephsy option 1 (and by necessity 6) are currently a total no-go for you, is that correct?<br /> <br /> Does anyone else have suggestions or comments? Am I going about this all wrong? I have no options that would be a breaker for me, but my personal preferences lie with 4 or 3, but again, certainly not opposed to the others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1705,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1705-okami","user":"Okami","date":". 05-27-2015, 03:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1705-okami","name":"Okami","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1705_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T12:41:38-07:00","id":530231,"title":"","content":"I'm happy with any of those options. 1 and 6 are out since Ephsy is not interested in that. If 2 or 3, I will play an Irraka Hunter in Darkness. If 4 or 5, I will play a Wolf-Blooded.<br /> <br /> I don't want to put words in Blue Biscut's mouth, so please correct me if I'm wrong, but it sounded like he was interested in the idea of running through hunting the Totem and in the possibility of running a Tribal Initiation for a young Werewolf, which would probably fit best with option 4. While I don't personally have a preference for any of these options, I support anything that inspires the ST or makes their job easier. It's also worth noting that option 4 gives us a couple of built-in objectives, which is always a good thing in my book.<br /> <br /> EDIT: It might also be a good idea to PM Ephsy - they may not be reading this thread any more if they gave up on the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 05-27-2015, 03:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T12:54:22-07:00","id":530242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/525133-lfg-werewolf-the-forsaken-2ed?p=530231#post530231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm happy with any of those options. 1 and 6 are out since Ephsy is not interested in that. If 2 or 3, I will play an Irraka Hunter in Darkness. If 4 or 5, I will play a Wolf-Blooded.<br /> <br /> I don't want to put words in Blue Biscut's mouth, so please correct me if I'm wrong, but it sounded like he was interested in the idea of running through hunting the Totem and in the possibility of running a Tribal Initiation for a young Werewolf, which would probably fit best with option 4. While I don't personally have a preference for any of these options, I support anything that inspires the ST or makes their job easier. It's also worth noting that option 4 gives us a couple of built-in objectives, which is always a good thing in my book.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I agree with you on four, what do the rest of you think? <br /> <br /> Also:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/525133-lfg-werewolf-the-forsaken-2ed?p=530231#post530231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT: It might also be a good idea to PM Ephsy - they may not be reading this thread any more if they gave up on the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Done.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1705-okami","name":"Okami","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1705_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T13:10:31-07:00","id":530253,"title":"","content":"I'm happy with any scenario, though if I had to choose a preference it would be 4 or 5. Literally have no problem with any scenario, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T14:07:29-07:00","id":530302,"title":"","content":"While it's true that I've expressed my interest in running a Tribal Initiation, it's by no means something I want to &quot;force&quot; you any of you through if you aren't intersted. Since Ephsy expressed preferance for starting already as a pack, if no one else explicitely has something against that I'd prefer to run it that way then.<br /> <br /> As for the Totem/Wolf-Blooded thing, both provide good motivations for the starting scenario, but they are by no means the only thing possible. Besides, wether or not they start play as a nuzusul or not depends on Charlaquin, and they seemed to be having troble with detailing the character, if I got things right.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/138-bluebiscuit","name":"BlueBiscuit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T14:17:35-07:00","id":530312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BlueBiscuit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/525133-lfg-werewolf-the-forsaken-2ed?p=530302#post530302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While it's true that I've expressed my interest in running a Tribal Initiation, it's by no means something I want to &quot;force&quot; you any of you through if you aren't intersted. Since Ephsy expressed preferance for starting already as a pack, if no one else explicitely has something against that I'd prefer to run it that way then.<br /> <br /> As for the Totem/Wolf-Blooded thing, both provide good motivations for the starting scenario, but they are by no means the only thing possible. Besides, wether or not they start play as a nuzusul or not depends on Charlaquin, and they seemed to be having troble with detailing the character, if I got things right.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was at first, but I got a handle on her <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. So I've got two characters ready to go, the starting scenario will determine which one I play - Irraka if we want to go fully pre-established, Wolf-Blooded if bringing a new character into the Pack is something the rest of the group is interested in playing. I'm quite happy with both characters at this point and don't have a preference one way or the other. I do think hunting down the Totem (which we would presumably build out-of-character beforehand) and/or introducing a young nuzusul into the fold does give us a bit of direction to start out with, but if anyone doesn't like the sound of that, I'm just as happy playing an established pack.<br /> <br /> Also, there's been a lot of &quot;they&quot;s used in the last few posts and while they is useful as a gender-neutral pronoun, I'm just going to throw it out there that I go by she/her if that makes it easier.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T14:30:18-07:00","id":530320,"title":"","content":"I also feel that I have to apologise for my tardiness in posting the setting outline, which I feel is partly resposible for the lack of direction you mentioned, but between feeling unwell and losing like 60% of what I had written to my laptop being uncooperative, it's been a fairly annoying couple of days.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/138-bluebiscuit","name":"BlueBiscuit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avat