ue":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T21:18:25-07:00","id":530625,"title":"","content":"Ephsy made the excellent suggestion to me that I could make my Wolf-Blooded part of the extended pack and effectively play both, which I feel rather silly for not thinking of myself. I do still like the idea of Rachel (my Wolf-Blooded) going through her First Change in-game, and at that point I might consider retiring Tom (my werewolf) and making her my primary character. But doing it this way to start with does sidestep a lot of potential issues.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T22:16:18-07:00","id":530698,"title":"","content":"Awesome, great solution and I do feel a little silly for not seeing it either. The whole notion of extended pack is something I still need to keep in mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1705-okami","name":"Okami","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1705_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T23:18:29-07:00","id":530714,"title":"","content":"By the way, I'm putting the finishing touches on both my characters now (I'll post them when I get home from work tomorrow), and a couple of questions came up while I was doing Aspirations. Since the original pitch involved us moving into the city, I assume we haven't staked claim to a territory yet? Would &quot;Clear out a territory for the pack&quot; and &quot;Form a locus on the pack's territory&quot; be appropriate aspirations? Also, since we don't have a Totem yet, obviously we don't have the Totem's Aspiration as a Pack Aspiration yet. Would &quot;Acquire a Totem&quot; be appropriate for a Pack Aspiration, then?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-28T00:08:10-07:00","id":530726,"title":"","content":"Indeed, you would be a pack formed relatively recently, and you wouldn't have claimed a territory <i>or </i>bound a Totem yet. And yes &quot;Acquire Totem&quot; is an absolutely appropriate Pack Aspiration. After I post the city writeup (I swear, you'll see it in the next few hours, or I'm not blue anymore <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />) and we're done with Pack creation properly we'll see talk about what sort of Totem you want, as well as the kind of territory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/138-bluebiscuit","name":"BlueBiscuit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-28T08:13:35-07