mi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/525133-lfg-werewolf-the-forsaken-2ed?p=531068#post531068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I figured she taught most of it to my other character, so she has to know it.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can burn merit points in either Shadowbind or Shadowcall, makes fetish crafting easier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-28T12:12:36-07:00","id":531193,"title":"","content":"Got my characters finished and ready to upload. <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B0KDN_qcgXvwaDItWldESDRkQ1U/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Here's Tom</a> and <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B0KDN_qcgXvwbGtOZ1QxemtuUEU/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Here's Rachel</a> and the other pack members.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Oh, I forgot to mention. When I was working on Rachel as a primary character I had planned to give her Fugue as a Persistent Condition that triggered when her Shape Shifted Tell kicked in. That's what the blackouts stuff is all about. There wasn't a space for Conditions on the Pack Members sheet, but is that still cool?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 05-28-2015, 03:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-28T13:43:47-07:00","id":531237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/525133-lfg-werewolf-the-forsaken-2ed?p=531186#post531186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You can burn merit points in either Shadowbind or Shadowcall, makes fetish crafting easier.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Didnt know about those, and I like them, I think I'll keep where her merits are for now and save up for the rites.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1705-okami","name":"Okami","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1705_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-28T14:21:39-07:00","id":531255,"title":"","content":"Alright then, after losing all that I had written down to a sudden reboot of my pc, I've mostly given up on the Hunting grounds style writing. This is mostly a write up on the city itself, the Uratha/criminal/supernatural part of it is upcoming.<br /> <br /> Willipa Bay is centered on a sheltered peninsula jutting into the mouth of the Albian River, with access to eponimous Bay and its islands, built mainly three hills, modest in size if compared to the surrounding mountains, but still quite steep. The city has over time spread to the western outer peninsula and along the south of the riverbank eastward as well as pushing south towards the mountains.<br /> The Downtown area of the city is towards the waterfront, the early center of Willipa's livelihood and activity. Royal Hill, the northernmost of the city\u2019s three main hills, lives up to its name with some of the most expensive real estate in Willipa. To the south rise University Hill, home of Willipa Bay University (WBU), and Sunset Hill, bordering the Red River. As the hills level out into a broad valley, the neighborhoods give way to the Eastern District and Lakeside, curving around Lake Vallee, an artificial lake formed by the Red River Dam.<br /> For many years, the major businesses in Willipa Bay were the fishing and lumber industries, alongside the various various mining companies working in the gem-rich Atlas Mountains. Recently however, Willipa has gone through a long economic slump as the local paper and forestry industries cut back on their operations and closed mills, while at the same time the fishing industry declined. This has caused an increase in the unemployment and crime rates. Efforts have been made in the last few years to attract new businesses to Willipa, in particular high-tech companies, While there has been some success, specifically with including computers, software, and aviation companies, it has been slow going.<br /> <br /> Neighborhoods (To be expanded upon) Here are a few bullet points:<br /> <b>Lakeside</b>: the &quot;new money&quot; neighboorhood, eccentric people live here<br /> <b>Crown Heights</b>: on Royal Hill, expensive, the &quot;old money&quot; neighborhood.<br /> <b>Eastern Distric</b>: actually south of downtown, Asian part of down, mainly Chinese and Japanese, with others in minor numbers (Korean, Vietnamese, etc)<br /> <b>Concord Row</b>: downtown area, shopping district.<br /> <b>Southern Shore</b>: suburban area, ethnically diverse, but slowly turning bad.<br /> <br /> Locations of Interest (to be expande as well):<br /> Willipa Bay suffered early flooding problems, which led to the city administration literally covering over and building on top of the old central part of the city in the lowlands. This created an \u201c<b>Undercity</b>&quot; where buildings and even streets from the 1800s are preserved beneath the current downtown area. A small part of it, known as The Maze has been properly mapped and turned into something of a tourist attraction. Beyond the lighted, well-trodden areas of the Maze, the Undercity conceals some hazards. Rotted floors, collapsing ceilings, fetid water, vermin packs, fugitive criminals, violent lunatics, and more dangers all lie just past the souvenir stands.<br /> <br /> Willipa Bay's <b>Riverfront</b> is still quite active as a port; much of the shipping has shifted eastward along the river and westward towards the outer peninsula, leaving much of the downtown waterfront area to piers dedicated to shopping, pleasure craft, and tourism. The more unsavory sorts trade is just as active, and if one knows where to look and who to talk to, they can find that money can buy many things here.<br /> <br /> The<b> Lakeside</b> area was originally\u2014in addition to being nowhere near a lake\u2014sparsely populated, save for a few gem miners working a few smaller claims. When those finally petered out in early 20th century, there was some talk of what to make of the area, but no real action was taken until the Great Depression. Then in 1933, under the Works Progress Administration, work began on the Red River Dam Project. When it was completed, the present Lake Vallee was formed. Today, Lakeside remains the place in Willipa where people who\u2019ve just gotten the means to realize their dreams congregate. Its residents tend to be outside-the-box thinkers whose lack of patience with rules and convention got them where they are, and thus refuse to conform now.<br /> <br /> Questions are welcomed, question help me flesh out stuff.<br /> <br /> Edit:<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/525133-lfg-werewolf-the-forsaken-2ed?p=531193#post531193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT: Oh, I forgot to mention. When I was working on Rachel as a primary character I had planned to give her Fugue as a Persistent Condition that triggered when her Shape Shifted Tell kicked in. That's what the blackouts stuff is all about. There wasn't a space for Conditions on the Pack Members sheet, but is that still cool?</div> </div> </div> </div>Cool, I'll add a note to remind myself of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":138,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/138-bluebiscuit","user":"BlueBiscuit","date":". 05-29-2015, 06:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/138-bluebiscuit","name":"BlueBiscuit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-28T14:27:19-07:00","id":531260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BlueBiscuit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/525133-lfg-werewolf-the-forsaken-2ed?p=531255#post531255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright then, after losing all that I had written down to a sudden reboot of my pc, I've mostly given up on the Hunting grounds still writing. This is mostly a write up on the city itself, the Uratha/criminal/supernatural part of it is upcoming.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really like what I'm seeing so far, sorry about all the work that you did lose, have you tried writing in a google doc as opposed to what processor your using? It would update in real time and that way you wouldn't lose things to sudden shut-downs.<br /> <br /> Hmm, my initial questions seem to be regarding the upcoming stuff, however, I love this &quot;Undercity&quot; idea, one thing I'm also curious about though, is what buildings <i>weren't</i> built over? Which ones are historic buildings and what is their history? Are some of them supposedly 'haunted'? etc. I ask because I've lived in two places thus far that have still had buildings and places hanging around after a hundred years or so, and not only is their history interesting, it leaves lots of potential for spirits/ghosts/whathaveyou. Just some food for thought.<br /> <br /> The two buildings oddly enough were a theater for stage performance that doubled as an emergency hospital during the Influenza Epidemic (I still remember the photos of coffins lining the alleyways just outside). Also a theater for cinema, though that one has been just a theater.<br /> <br /> EDIT; As an off topic note, does anyone else feel like the split between academics and science is weird? Like that since Academics is supposed to represent your characters overall higher education and research experience they could have just folded science into that and left the rest up to specializations? Take my character for example, I see her with heavy education in chemistry, which goes hand in hand with academics, but to mechanically reflect that in skills I dropped academics entirely (which gives the impression she doesnt have a higher education) in order to put three in Science. It just feels inefficient. Anyone have a different perspective on the matter?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1705,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1705-okami","user":"Okami","date":". 05-28-2015, 05:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1705-okami","name":"Okami","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1705_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-28T14:46:22-07:00","id":531267,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0BxK0La5plUm8QmJ2NzFFTUowVkU/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Updated character sheet.</a> I got rid of Contacts: Black Market Dealers since it seems Okami's character already has that covered. Again, will happily drop a dot of Allies for Totem merit. Last decision to make is whether she's an Iron Master or Storm Lord. I'm leaning toward Storm Lords for two reasons. One: Strings of the Heart is too good a merit to pass up and feels central to her character (though Sounds of the City is pretty in character for her as well). And Two: I can't imagine her thinking of humans as the most worthy prey. In my head she sort of considers them pawns. The Storm Lord Ban is very up her alley.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The pros for Iron Master is pretty much just the Knowledge Gift and Sounds of the City is pretty cool. She is also very focused on connections in the human world, which is very Iron Master. That last part is pretty key though.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I also have become a disciple of Ephsy's genius and just used my <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0BxK0La5plUm8aVRCWlZKTTJvZlU/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">other character as my wolf blooded</a>. &quot;Romeo&quot; Remy St. Croix aka Pretty Boy St. Croix.<br /> <br /> He's a fighter who basically wins fights because of his advanced healing and the ability to throw a half decent hook. He's famous for taking punches but never messing up his pretty face. He's been an acquaintance of Madeleine's for some time because everyone loves him around town and he can be a useful source of information, but sometimes she think he's more trouble than he's worth. She also doesn't find him as charming as he himself does. His aspirations were jokes at first but I like them so I'm probably keeping them as is.<br /> <br /> Its also come to my attention that both my human characters are very similar to characters you guys already have (Tony and Cibo), I'll start trying to think up some other guys to take their place or at least changing their skills up a bit.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-28T15:07:43-07:00","id":531275,"title":"","content":"I'm not married to Tony, I could come up with another human character if you want to keep Two-Fingers. Tony Two-Fingers actually has a nice ring to it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> It seems like Storm Lords are a better fit if you can't see her considering humans most dangerous. While leveraging human connections <i>is</i> very Iron-Master, it's also very Elodoth.<br /> <br /> Also, I noticed we've both got the Hunting Ground Rite. That's not a problem necessarily, since it's a Pack Rite and we can use teamwork. But it might be worth considering one of us taking something else to diversify our abilities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 05-28-2015, 06:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-28T15:27:39-07:00","id":531311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Okami</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/525133-lfg-werewolf-the-forsaken-2ed?p=531260#post531260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The two buildings oddly enough were a theater for stage performance that doubled as an emergency hospital during the Influenza Epidemic (I still remember the photos of coffins lining the alleyways just outside).</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"http://cdn.meme.am/instances/55674709.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> For real though, theaters and hospitals are both notorious for frequently being haunted.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Okami</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/525133-lfg-werewolf-the-forsaken-2ed?p=531260#post531260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT; As an off topic note, does anyone else feel like the split between academics and science is weird? Like that since Academics is supposed to represent your characters overall higher education and research experience they could have just folded science into that and left the rest up to specializations? Take my character for example, I see her with heavy education in chemistry, which goes hand in hand with academics, but to mechanically reflect that in skills I dropped academics entirely (which gives the impression she doesnt have a higher education) in order to put three in Science. It just feels inefficient. Anyone have a different perspective on the matter?</div> </div> </div> </div>You could say the same of Academics and Medicine. And Medicine and Science. But anyway, I don't think Academics necessarily represents overall level of education (or, it shouldn't, anyway). I think of it more like the Humanities Skill (which would be a better name for it, imo).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-28T15:37:55-07:00","id":531320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Okami</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/525133-lfg-werewolf-the-forsaken-2ed?p=531260#post531260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I really like what I'm seeing so far, sorry about all the work that you did lose, have you tried writing in a google doc as opposed to what processor your using? It would update in real time and that way you wouldn't lose things to sudden shut-downs.<br /> <br /> Hmm, my initial questions seem to be regarding the upcoming stuff, however, I love this &quot;Undercity&quot; idea, one thing I'm also curious about though, is what buildings <i>weren't</i> built over? Which ones are historic buildings and what is their history? Are some of them supposedly 'haunted'? etc. I ask because I've lived in two places thus far that have still had buildings and places hanging around after a hundred years or so, and not only is their history interesting, it leaves lots of potential for spirits/ghosts/whathaveyou. Just some food for thought.<br /> <br /> The two buildings oddly enough were a theater for stage performance that doubled as an emergency hospital during the Influenza Epidemic (I still remember the photos of coffins lining the alleyways just outside). Also a theater for cinema, though that one has been just a theater.<br /> <br /> EDIT; As an off topic note, does anyone else feel like the split between academics and science is weird? Like that since Academics is supposed to represent your characters overall higher education and research experience they could have just folded science into that and left the rest up to specializations? Take my character for example, I see her with heavy education in chemistry, which goes hand in hand with academics, but to mechanically reflect that in skills I dropped academics entirely (which gives the impression she doesnt have a higher education) in order to put three in Science. It just feels inefficient. Anyone have a different perspective on the matter?</div> </div> </div> </div>If my suspicions are correct, the Undercity will have two broad divisions: the modernized half, which will be gentrified to hell and back, and spiritually be dominated by Technologicals, Greeds, and smaller shop and structure spirits, and the historical half, which will be inundated with squatters (maybe a few Unclean, if Blue's so inclined), urban scavengers, and any number of shadow cultures, while the Hisil there will reflect how disused those areas are, and will likely be our main source of Hosts, Claimed, or even Maeljin and their minions.<br /> <br /> IMHO, Academics is more about a character's ability to process information than a measure of training. So having a high rating in an applied discipline like Science or Computers or Crafts but no Academics, to me, says that your character has a lot more hard-earned, firsthand experience in a given discipline than they would have gotten through book-learning and rote memorization. In short, you're less Hermione Granger, more Seamus Finnegan, when describing how you learn things (I wouldn't be surprised if worrying about the state of your hair/eyebrows would be a character quirk, tbh).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-28T16:50:01-07:00","id":531394,"title":"","content":"I swear to Jesus I was planning on naming my guy something with Fingers. I just couldn't think of the epithet exactly so I left it alone. I definitely want a sort of fence/black market dealer on her roster though so if you have any other ideas for your peripherals I will gladly accept Two Fingers. As far as Hunting Grounds I am super flexible on that one. I can't really see any rites that aren't already represented in other packmates except either Moon's Mad Love or Wellspring. I might just switch to Wellspring, I'll think about it. Let me know if you have any suggestions.<br /> <br /> And yeah, I think the Storm Lords is going to really be her final Tribe, thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-28T17:03:29-07:00","id":531398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/525133-lfg-werewolf-the-forsaken-2ed?p=531394#post531394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I swear to Jesus I was planning on naming my guy something with Fingers.</div> </div> </div> </div>You did, Two-Fingers is the name written on the sheet you posted.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/525133-lfg-werewolf-the-forsaken-2ed?p=531394#post531394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As far as Hunting Grounds I am super flexible on that one. I can't really see any rites that aren't already represented in other packmates except either Moon's Mad Love or Wellspring. I might just switch to Wellspring, I'll think about it. Let me know if you have any suggestions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wellspring is a good option. You could also always take Sacred Hunt for the seeing Ridden benefit. Or, if you were considering dropping a dot of Allies anyway, you could take Raiment of the Storm, which is only available to Storm Lords.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-28T17:47:21-07:00","id":531453,"title":"","content":"Hm. Yeah, Sacred Hunt actually makes the most sense, actually. Raiment of the Storm is pretty cool as well, but I really want that dot in totem so I probably won't give it up.<br /> <br /> Hahaha, I guess I did actually add the name to the sheet. I was so stupefied when I thought you had come up with the same name as I did. Like, bewildered. Now it all makes sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-28T19:47:38-07:00","id":531572,"title":"","content":"I assume that we'll need a writeup of how we conduct the Rites we have, eh? I have some ideas.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I've add the following to my sheet, which is reflected in the file I linked:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Banish: Will carries a pack of black felt markers, which he and his pack use to mark the boundaries of where they stand with leering eyes. Each then stands back to back in silence, compelled only to howl at the presence of an interloper (Composure + Occult)</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Bottle Spirit: Will keeps a bottle of corn whiskey, half filled with ash culled from Hell Bank Notes and Prayer Lanterns, which he ignites when invoking this Rite. (Presence + Occult)</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Totemic Empowerment: (reserving until we know what type of totem we want, but it will likely be Stamina + Empathy)</span><br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":1959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","user":"Hexmeister Vic","date":". 05-29-2015, 12:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-28T19:49:23-07:00","id":531573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/525133-lfg-werewolf-the-forsaken-2ed?p=531311#post531311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For real though, theaters and hospitals are both notorious for frequently being haunted.</div> </div> </div> </div>This one was both, clearly double the fun. (If I recall correctly they did tell us about some supposed hauntings during performances but my memory is cloudy.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/525133-lfg-werewolf-the-forsaken-2ed?p=531311#post531311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could say the same of Academics and Medicine. And Medicine and Science. But anyway, I don't think Academics necessarily represents overall level of education (or, it shouldn't, anyway). I think of it more like the Humanities Skill (which would be a better name for it, imo).</div> </div> </div> </div>Thats how I look at it too, what bothers me is in the book it reads; <br /> <br /> &quot;Academics is a broad Skill representing your character\u2019s<br /> higher education and knowledge of the arts and humanities.&quot;<br /> <br /> -Werewolf The Forsaken: Second Edition, Page 154<br /> <br /> but yeah, as I said, I personally define it like you do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1705-okami","name":"Okami","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1705_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-28T19:55:09-07:00","id":531576,"title":"","content":"I have Gideon's character sheet ready, but is it okay if I present it in a way that doesn't use Google Drive?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/233-daydreamer","name":"Daydreamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"193"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-28T20:34:52-07:00","id":531652,"title":"","content":"*shrug* what ever works.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-28T23:30:42-07:00","id":531756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daydreamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/525133-lfg-werewolf-the-forsaken-2ed?p=531576#post531576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have Gideon's character sheet ready, but is it okay if I present it in a way that doesn't use Google Drive?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, I know you want to keep your backstory a secret for now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/138-bluebiscuit","name":"BlueBiscuit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T16:32:04-07:00","id":532496,"title":"","content":"Ladies, gents and anyone in between: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B6vxY2L7VdTZdkNDSEgtckUzVFE/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">This is Mal </a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T16:59:19-07:00","id":532567,"title":"","content":"Nice! So now that we've got everyone's sheets (I think?) we should start building ties, yes?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T16:59:38-07:00","id":532573,"title":"","content":"Okay, hell with it. I made a dummy account, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=0B1sYlMEIRzbbanJhZ2VULVJ4MjQ&amp;authuser=0\" target=\"_blank\">so here's Gideon</a>.<br /> <br /> Edit: I'm not sure about that Parkour. I don't know how well it fits him. I may end up giving it up for something else, maybe another dot of Tactical Shifting or a Language.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":233,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/233-daydreamer","user":"Daydreamer","date":". 05-29-2015, 08:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/233-daydreamer","name":"Daydreamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"193"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T17:08:03-07:00","id":532591,"title":"","content":"How many free totem points we get?<br /> <br /> Edit: Do we need the actual language merit to speak First Tongue fluently?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":576,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","user":"Ephsy","date":". 05-29-2015, 08:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T17:34:48-07:00","id":532601,"title":"","content":"It states in the book that all werewolves get first tongue for free. All the sheets are now done, though I need to edit mine, still need to add backstory, allocate the auspice skill, and that should be it. So yeah we can definitely get started with the character ties.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1705-okami","name":"Okami","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1705_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T18:06:13-07:00","id":532618,"title":"","content":"I'll start. I notice Tom and Gideon have a lot in common, including the fact that they're both homeless (I assume, based on the &quot;Drifter&quot; concept, anyway). So I'd say Tom is probably more relaxed around him. He's normally pretty guarded, but with Gideon he allows himself to let lose, share stories of experiences on the road, that kind of thing. He might also want to try to convince him to join the Hunters in Darkness, since the choice not to join a Tribe probably seems strange to Tom.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T19:44:52-07:00","id":532690,"title":"","content":"I think the person Madeleine has the most in common with is Will (both Elodoth, both Wallflowers, both have a history of using their skills to exploit people), I imagine they'll find themselves on the same side of any disagreements that arrive in the pack. Elizabeth and Madeleine both have similar connections and <i>I think </i>operate in similar spheres though with different goals, perhaps, so I think could probably be closest. <br /> <br /> The rest I'm not sure about. Madeleine is very about not getting her hands dirty, so to speak, and so that might be at odds with some of the rest of the pack.<br /> <br /> By the way, we have 3 Lone Wolf Bones and 2 Wallflowers so this pack is going to be a bunch of people trying to solve problems themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T19:55:46-07:00","id":532700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/525133-lfg-werewolf-the-forsaken-2ed?p=532690#post532690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the way, we have 3 Lone Wolf Bones and 2 Wallflowers so this pack is going to be a bunch of people trying to solve problems themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Haha yeah, that might be a bit of a problem... I guess I could see Tom as a Guru, in that case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T20:36:11-07:00","id":532719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/525133-lfg-werewolf-the-forsaken-2ed?p=532690#post532690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the way, we have 3 Lone Wolf Bones and 2 Wallflowers so this pack is going to be a bunch of people trying to solve problems themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Funny thing, that; I chose a custom Bone that gives Willpower when you help packmates sort out their problems. This should be fun.<br /> <br /> So, about my backstory. It's easier for me to write it up here than transfer everything to a new, 4-page sheet.<br /> <br /> Gideon used to travel with another Ghost Wolf who went by the name Satchel. Other than that, he is known to the Uratha of Willipa Bay only by rumor. He's killed an unknown number of the Pure and seen things some werewolves would be surprised to learn even existed. He's displayed a level of underhandedness that few would ever expect from a Rahu, as well as a knack for setting booby traps--he killed at least one of his Pure victims without ever getting blood on his claws. No werewolf without a tribe or pack could be admired, and Gideon's un-Rahu tactics have earned him his fair share of scorn. But he is grudgingly respected for one fact: after all this time alone, he's still alive.<br /> <br /> He came to Willipa Bay not long ago and started putting out feelers for a pack willing to take in a rootless Ghost Wolf. In Tom, he found a kindred spirit (Tom might have been the one to introduce him to the other wolves). He shows a lot of respect for Mal's team spirit and Will's desire for redemption. Elizabeth's talk about creating a safe place resonates with him; he wants to start living in just one place where he doesn't always have to be on his guard. He's not quite sure how to act around Madeleine, though: if you didn't know better, you'd think he was suspicious of her.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/233-daydreamer","name":"Daydreamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"193"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T20:37:17-07:00","id":532720,"title":"","content":"So, I'm thinking Tom is probably both impressed with and a bit baffled by by Elizabeth and Will. They're clearly both adept with technology and spirits, both of which are a bit beyond his frame of reference. He definitely appreciates having someone with their skills in the pack, but doesn't fully understand what it is they do. He might come to them for help with things that they can't actually do much about, because he's so illiterate in their fields he doesn't really know what they are or aren't capable of.<br /> <br /> Madeline's connection to the police makes Tom uneasy. In his experience, police have only ever meant bad news, so he consciously avoids any involvement with that particular branch of her web.<br /> <br /> Tom probably sees Mal as his foil in some ways. Where Tom is subtle, Mal is strong. Where Tom is most at home blending into the background as just one more wild animal or face in the crowd, Mal is unapologetically present and direct. Tom enjoys the way Mal complements his own abilities in combat, but he's also secretly a little bit afraid of him. The fact that he's a Blood Talon doesn't help. But he takes comfort in knowing that at least Mal is on his side.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T21:27:05-07:00","id":532746,"title":"","content":"Will thirsts for knowledge, so he tends to follow Elizabeth's lead in delicate matters. He works hard to scrub some of the red out of his ledger, but old habits die hard, so he can't help but view Mal and Gideon as a fire and forget weapon and an insurance policy, respectively, but he refuses to rationalize such possibilities as essential to his ideals. He admires Madeline's conviction, and bets that they'd clean up the town, left to their own devices. Tom is a bit of a mystery to him, though. Might be worth investing time with, he imagines. He sees a lot of himself in Emily though, a lot of the same issues, if not the same coping strategies.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T21:39:47-07:00","id":532753,"title":"","content":"I'm gonna change Mal's Bone to Hedonist. His physical touchstone is gonna be <i>the sponsor</i>. I'm undecided in spiritual. Maybe totem, but we don't have one yet.<br /> <br /> The way I see Mal is like the one who gets his hands dirty, his talons bloodied (pun intended). The one who bears the burden of killing, or outright murdering when the Hunt calls for it. The one who snaps the bones. His training in medicine was deliberately provided by tribemates, so he'd know exactly where to strike efficiently.<br /> <br /> He can respect Gideon's methods, but doesn't shares them. To him, the kill must be up close and personal.<br /> <br /> He takes Tom's reservations for granted, he's made it sort of a personal mission to bully him, in order to get him to stand up for himself. Either Tom will, or he's is gonna Kuruth around Mal. Mal considers either outcome acceptable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T23:40:22-07:00","id":532961,"title":"","content":"So, I gave Ephsy's Blood and Bone thread a more thorough read, and I think I'm going to change Tom's Blood to Relentless and his Bone to Maker.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 05-30-2015, 02:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-30T00:25:49-07:00","id":532972,"title":"","content":"I should make one for new Touchstones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-30T13:58:41-07:00","id":533600,"title":"","content":"So we should probably start brainstorming ideas for what kind of Totem we want to go after. We've got, what, 7 dots to work with? So that's a Rank 1 spirit with either a 3/3/1 or 3/2/2 spread and 2 Numina. So clearly we're starting with a fairly weak spirit and nurturing it to become something greater. Our pack seems to all be onboard with the idea of making Willapa a safer space, so I'd assume something that resonates with protection or fortification?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-30T14:06:12-07:00","id":533602,"title":"","content":"Well, we have I think we have allotted 6 or 7 dots in totem (I'm removing Fixer for a dot or two in Totem, still deliberating) and then we start with 6 dots in totem according to character creation rules, (assuming our ST doesn't have other plans) so I think we have at least 12. Unless I'm doing the calculations wrong","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-30T14:17:53-07:00","id":533622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/525133-lfg-werewolf-the-forsaken-2ed?p=533600#post533600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So we should probably start brainstorming ideas for what kind of Totem we want to go after. We've got, what, 7 dots to work with? So that's a Rank 1 spirit with either a 3/3/1 or 3/2/2 spread and 2 Numina. So clearly we're starting with a fairly weak spirit and nurturing it to become something greater. Our pack seems to all be onboard with the idea of making Willapa a safer space, so I'd assume something that resonates with protection or fortification?</div> </div> </div> </div>Safer for what? For whom? My character <b>is</b> a thug. Not a vigilante.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-30T14:45:00-07:00","id":533655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/525133-lfg-werewolf-the-forsaken-2ed?p=533602#post533602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, we have I think we have allotted 6 or 7 dots in totem (I'm removing Fixer for a dot or two in Totem, still deliberating) and then we start with 6 dots in totem according to character creation rules, (assuming our ST doesn't have other plans) so I think we have at least 12. Unless I'm doing the calculations wrong</div> </div> </div> </div>I think we all included our free Totem dot on our character sheets. So I count 8 dots (9 if you drop Fixer for Totem). 1 from Elizabeth, 2 from Gideon, 2 or 3 from Madeline, 1 from Mal, 1 from Tom, and 1 from Will. So actually that just makes Rank 2, with a 4/4/1, 4/3/2, or 3/3/3 Attribute split and 2 Numina.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/525133-lfg-werewolf-the-forsaken-2ed?p=533622#post533622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Safer for what? For whom? My character <b>is</b> a thug. Not a vigilante.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was going off of this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daydreamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/525133-lfg-werewolf-the-forsaken-2ed?p=532719#post532719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Elizabeth's talk about creating a safe place resonates with him; he wants to start living in just one place where he doesn't always have to be on his guard.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which would also be a goal important to Tom. Since that's half the pack, I don't have much detail about two of the remaining three's backgrounds, and the last doesn't seem like he would be *opposed* to that goal, I figured I'd throw the idea out there and count on the rest of the group using &quot;yes, and&quot; to build from there. If that idea doesn't appeal to you, no problem, have you got any other suggestions?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-30T14:57:01-07:00","id":533662,"title":"","content":"Ah, I see. Of course that makes sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-30T15:02:22-07:00","id":533664,"title":"","content":"Sorry, correction: 3 Numina. And at 9 dots we would have 3 experiences to spend on the Totem Benefit.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I'd also be willing to drop Nowhere to Run for another dot or two of Totem if that's something the group would want.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 05-30-2015, 06:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-30T15:51:27-07:00","id":533709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/525133-lfg-werewolf-the-forsaken-2ed?p=532720#post532720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Madeline's connection to the police makes Tom uneasy. In his experience, police have only ever meant bad news, so he consciously avoids any involvement with that particular branch of her web.</div> </div> </div> </div>In regards to this and the members of the pack who don't really like having to deal with the police, the primary way Madeleine's relationship with the police translates for the pack is having them turn a blind eye to the goings-on of the group, so even those that are hesitant to be associated however loosely with the authorities might be happy to reap those benefits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-30T16:04:56-07:00","id":533740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/525133-lfg-werewolf-the-forsaken-2ed?p=533655#post533655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was going off of this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daydreamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/525133-lfg-werewolf-the-forsaken-2ed?p=532719#post532719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Elizabeth's talk about creating a safe place resonates with him; he wants to start living in just one place where he doesn't always have to be on his guard.</div> </div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>Um, Elizabeth's goal of a Safe Place was the merit, like a hidey/supply hole for herself in case things get bad or a wounded pack member can't make it back to base, not a safe... <i>place</i>.<br /> <br /> But she'd stil mention that anyway! But more in course of talking about the territory as a whole, you know, Iron Master Oath and all that.<br /> <br /> &quot;Hey, this local drug-dealing gang is fucking up this entire tennament block and drawing all kinds of nasty murder and violence spirits, they gotta go.&quot; Kinds of stuff.<br /> <br /> Mal she'll be very wary around until she see's him in action, he may act like a thug but if it's in the right way she'll see it as an asset.<br /> <br /> Elizabeth herself isn't above outright eliminating what she see's as a danger to the pack and their territory, human or not. Provided elimination will have the correct response she's looking for. She's incredibly methodical in her evaluations, and she naturally see's managing a territory very much like a sort of experiment. Certain actions get certain responses, some desired some not. What's smart is doing what gets you the best response, whats foolish is acting without knowing what those responses are going to be (with the caveat that acting to observe the response is fine. In a nice, controlled, small scale setting).<br /> <br /> Unfortunately for her, as dispassionate and scientific as she likes to see her own behavior, being a shapeshifting rage-beast driven on a fundamental level by very intense passions more often than not lends a... <i>bias</i> to much of her work. As it turns out pushing out the gang by getting a member of the pack to pull some political strings might be the best option. But they have a slight in with the cops, could cause complications, and Elizabeth really has a hard time stomaching gangs, perhaps taking out a couple of members who are alone and making it look like the work of a rival faction in the other part of the city would be better. It's in these kind of situations where she'll need her pack to ground her (unless they're all for it, but Elizabeth would later come to regret such a decision, waaaaay too many uncontrollable variables in gang turf wars).<br /> <br /> Tom's background will surprise Elizabeth, given how dedicated he is to forwarding the pack and how steadily he'll work towards those goals, so she'll like that about him.<br /> <br /> Rachel will need watching over, in Elizabeth's mind, once the pack runs into her (speaking of, how are we handling the pack noticing her? Do they already? should we play that out? maybe they catch her during a &quot;blackout&quot; or stop by somewhere she works?) maybe a pooling of of resources to get her a better job. An on-the-cusp-of-first-change werewolf is not only a fellow Uratha but a target for the Pure, Spirits, Hunters, and other nasty things out there. In Elizabeth's mind people need a lot of things to work towards <s>being useful</s>, <s>an asset</s>, <s>not a fool</s>, actually being able to focus on their lives and living them the best they can. She knows, and she has a checklist, Rachel is missing a depressing amount of checks, and for a potential future packmate this simply will not do.<br /> <br /> Madeleine she will see as indispensable, but will worry her political ambitions might get in the way of taking care of the pack and their territory first, so she'll be wary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1705,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1705-okami","user":"Okami","date":". 05-30-2015, 07:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1705-okami","name":"Okami","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1705_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-30T16:44:10-07:00","id":533763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Okami</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/525133-lfg-werewolf-the-forsaken-2ed?p=533740#post533740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Um, Elizabeth's goal of a Safe Place was the merit, like a hidey/supply hole for herself in case things get bad or a wounded pack member can't make it back to base, not a safe... <i>place</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>........*facepalm* I'm sorry. In hindsight that should have been obvious, I don't know how I misinterpreted when that's literally the name of the Merit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Okami</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/525133-lfg-werewolf-the-forsaken-2ed?p=533740#post533740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rachel will need watching over, in Elizabeth's mind, once the pack runs into her (speaking of, how are we handling the pack noticing her? Do they already? should we play that out? maybe they catch her during a &quot;blackout&quot; or stop by somewhere she works?) maybe a pooling of of resources to get her a better job. An on-the-cusp-of-first-change werewolf is not only a fellow Uratha but a target for the Pure, Spirits, Hunters, and other nasty things out there. In Elizabeth's mind people need a lot of things to work towards <s>being useful</s>, <s>an asset</s>, <s>not a fool</s>, actually being able to focus on their lives and living them the best they can. She knows, and she has a checklist, Rachel is missing a depressing amount of checks, and for a potential future packmate this simply will not do.</div> </div> </div> </div>I figured we'd already know about her from the aftermath of her blackouts, since she's one of the extended pack members, but I would not be opposed to playing out learning of her in-game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 05-30-2015, 09:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-30T18:01:37-07:00","id":533826,"title":"","content":"Will is definitely a talk first, then sic the Rahus if they don't listen kind of character. Most likely, I'm going to want a totem that'll either make the group better at fighting as a unit, or better at socializing. Maybe we could get something more abstract? Like an Elemental or Conceptual?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-30T18:10:54-07:00","id":533834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/525133-lfg-werewolf-the-forsaken-2ed?p=533826#post533826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Will is definitely a talk first, then sic the Rahus if they don't listen kind of character. Most likely, I'm going to want a totem that'll ei