h the Air Elemental look. What else?</div> </div> </div> </div>Dement might be a decent choice, as would Rapture or Hallucination. Also, Seek feels right to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-02T01:48:31-07:00","id":536751,"title":"","content":"Depending on how aggressive you envision it to be, Drain may also be appropriate. Also, coming soon, the Tribes of Willipa Bay (both Pure and Forsaken), an overview of it's Hisil and the other inhabitants of the it's dark corners.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/138-bluebiscuit","name":"BlueBiscuit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-02T08:57:50-07:00","id":537109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/525133-lfg-werewolf-the-forsaken-2ed?p=536291#post536291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can't have Finesse 5 unless we get it up to 10 Totem dots.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd still choose Power over Resistance there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-02T12:08:18-07:00","id":537301,"title":"","content":"Have some more stuff on the surrounding of Willipa Bay, it's wilderness this time.<br /> <br /> Unlike more urbanized parts of the United States, Willipa Bay is relatively isolated: get outside of the city limits, and even the suburban neighborhoods quickly give way to Pacific rainforest, rolling foothills, and, eventually, the high peaks of the Atlas Mountains or the flat expanse of the Pacific Ocean.<br /> <br /> A broad swath of greenery stretching from the southeastern borders of Willipa Bay into the lowlands of the Atlas Mountains, the<b> Elysian Forest </b>is a local and national treasure. Large parts of the forest near the mountains are protected national parkland, safe from development to preserve wildlife habitats as well as their natural beauty. The Elysian Forest is part of the temperate rainforest region of North America, the largest temperate zone rainforest area in the world. It sees considerable annual rainfall (primarily in the winter rainy season) as well as heavy summertime fogs, which recirculate moisture on the forest floor. It is primarily made up of old-growth redwoods, Douglas fir, Sitka spruce, western hemlock, and the western red cedar. Heavy layers of moss, ferns, and similar undergrowth are common due to the moisture and richness of deadfalls and other decaying plant matter. It is also home to a wide variety of animal life as well, from Pacific Northwest species of elk and deer to foxes, bears, and timberwolves. Owls, eagles, and other hunting birds share nesting grounds with crows ravens, woodpeckers, flickers, and numerous smaller bird species. The rivers and streams have abundant life, from salmon and other fish to frogs and salamanders.<br /> <br /> The majestic <b>Atlas Mountains</b> surround the Willipa Bay region like a massive fence, stretching in a roughly north-south range some distance eastward of the peninsulas and the mouth of the Albian River. The Arcadian Peaks, forming the middle of the Outer Peninsula, are a spur of the Atlas Mountains, smaller than their eastern cousins. The natural barrier of the mountains keeps clouds and weather formations moving in from the ocean trapped over the Willipa Bay area, contributing to its famous rainy and often overcast weather. Precipitation in the upper reaches of the mountains is typically snow, the only regular snowfall in the region. Well over a hundred inches of snowfall in the high mountains is not unusual in one year, and the tallest Atlas Mountains remain snow-capped year-round.<br /> The Atlas Mountains are part of the Pacific \u201cRing of Fire\u201d formed by the meeting of two great continental plates. A great many of them are volcanic, although most of the volcanic mountains in the Atlas Range have been mostly dormant for decades, if not centuries, and eruptions are rare.<br /> Mount Stanley, named for one of the first explorers to reach the bay area, is the tallest and most visible peak in the Atlas Range. On a clear day, it is visible from across the Albian River area.<br /> <br /> I promise, the good stuff is coming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/138-bluebiscuit","name":"BlueBiscuit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-na